Console fonts shipped on the live image in addition to `kbd` and `terminus-font`
==============================================================================

Why they are here
-----------------
The installer's interface draws Ukrainian Cyrillic, Latin-1 accents for Spanish
and box-drawing at the same time. Of the 362 console fonts that `kbd` and
`terminus-font` install, only two families can do all of that at once: Terminus
(`ter-v*`) and `LatGrkCyr`. `terminus-font` looks like ten families but nine of
them (`ter-c`, `ter-d`, `ter-g`, `ter-h`, `ter-i`, `ter-k`, `ter-m`, `ter-p`,
`ter-u`) are ~262-glyph single-codepage subsets and cannot render a trilingual
interface by design. No package in Arch, Artix or Chaotic-AUR ships any other
console font — so the only way to offer a real choice is to carry these files.

What was changed, and how
-------------------------
A Linux console font holds exactly 512 glyphs; that is the kernel's ceiling and
every one of these was already at it. Missing characters were therefore added by
REUSING glyph slots the interface never asks for, and each new glyph was built
out of shapes the same font already draws — so nothing was drawn by hand and each
font keeps its own weight and proportions. `scripts/psf-patch.py` in the project
repository does this and is the exact provenance of these files:

  tui-*
      added ▀ ▄ ▌ (pure geometry: top, bottom and left half of the cell).

Every file was verified with `psfgettable` from `kbd`: 512 mappings each, and
the added codepoints present.

Upstream and licences
---------------------
  tui-*           "Artix TUI" / "Artix TUI Bold" — Terminus Font by Dimitar
                  Zhekov, OFL-1.1, WITH THREE GLYPHS ADDED and renamed.
                  https://terminus-font.sourceforge.net/       LICENSE.terminus

                  Terminus is OFL-1.1 with the Reserved Font Name "Terminus
                  Font". Clause 3 forbids a modified version from carrying that
                  name, so these copies are called something else. The change is
                  three glyphs — `▀ ▄ ▌` — added because the donation QR code is
                  half-block encoded and Terminus ships only `█ ░ ▒`; without
                  them the code drew as a field of holes no scanner could read.
                  Nothing else about the font was touched.


These licences cover the font files in this directory only. The installer itself
is Apache-2.0; see the project's own LICENSE.

The packaged Terminus ships unchanged and is not offered by the installer; the
renamed copies above are what the font screen lists. Where a font still cannot
draw the half blocks, the installer falls back to a full-block QR code (twice the
size, same modules) and only drops it when there is no room for either.
